  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Doing a boxCollider.Raycast() from an external point to a box collider will correctly detect the hit, but hit.point is always Vector3(0,0,0). FYI, Collider.RayCast should not be confused with Physics.Raycast. In my test, my BoxCollider and ray was far away from Vector3(0,0,0), so there is no way that this result is correct.\n\nCode to replicate:\n-------------------------------------------------------\nVRCPlayerApi.TrackingData trackingData = _localPlayer.GetTrackingData(VRCPlayerApi.TrackingDataType.Head);\nVector3 direction = trackingData.rotation * Vector3.forward;\nRay ray = new Ray(trackingData.position, direction);\nRaycastHit hit;\nif (_collider.Raycast(ray, out hit, 50f))\n{\n    Debug.Log(\"Raycast hit point: \" + hit.point.x + \", \" + hit.point.y + \", \" + hit.point.z);\n}\n-------------------------------------------------------\nOutput: Log - Raycast hit point: 0, 0, 0",
